From 17c63fe0621b03a4df5f0b9b5d8cc62367d9d0b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 3 <phase3@openwch.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 02:17:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] RISC-V: accept bare XW arch attributes in EVT assembly

Register XW with the version WCH's own assembler canonicalises to.  A bare
xw, whether spelled concatenated or with a separating underscore, comes
back as xw2p2 there -- in the $x mapping symbol, in -march=help, and in
the Tag_RISCV_arch string once attribute write-out is asked for -- while
an explicit xw2p0 or xw9p9 passes through untouched.  The common ISA
parser needs nothing beyond the table row for all of that.

This does not change what GCC produces for a bare -march=rv32imac_xw: GCC
writes its own arch string into the .s it hands to gas, and that string
already carries an explicit xw2p0, which gas preserves.  The two faces are
independent and both are tested.

Behavior specification:
  analysis/toolchain/wch-gcc-toolchain-survey.md sections 5.1 and 5.2
  ref/wch-isa-research/isa/custom/wch-custom-isa-reference.md section 4.1
Direct WCH 15.2.0 probes establish the bare-form canonicalisation, the
explicit-version passthrough and the -march=help entry.
